---
description: Standards for SQLAlchemy/PostgreSQL load layer
globs: src/load/**/*.py
alwaysApply: false
---

# Load Layer Rules

- Isolate SQLAlchemy engine/session creation from business logic.
- Use transactions explicitly and roll back cleanly on failures.
- Make load mode explicit (`append`, `replace`, or upsert strategy) and document it.
- Use chunked writes for large datasets when appropriate.
- Emit clear load metrics (rows processed, inserted, failed).

# Load Tests

- Cover successful insert path and DB failure/rollback path.
- Cover behavior for repeated loads according to selected idempotency strategy.
